From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:19:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: check for the PHY before powering up the
 host

The QMP UFS PHY takes its reset from the UFS host (resets = <&ufs_mem_hc 0>),
and the host takes the PHY (phys = <&ufs_mem_phy>). fw_devlink sees the cycle
and demotes the host->PHY link to sync-state-only, so the host can probe
before the PHY has bound.

When it does, ufshcd_pltfrm_init() first powers up the host: regulators,
clocks (including the GPLL4-sourced UFS clocks), all on. Only then does
ufs_qcom_init() reach devm_phy_get(), get -EPROBE_DEFER, and the whole lot is
switched back off, about 24 ms later.

On the KONKR Pocket FIT (SM8650) this happens on every boot, at the same time
as the async sdhci_msm probe of SDC2, the controller the board booted from.
In about half the boots the board then resets silently: a pstore console
catches both probes in flight as the last thing printed. With ufs-qcom kept
from probing (initcall_blacklist), 8 of 8 reboots came up clean; before that,
4 of 6 reset.

Check for the PHY at the top of probe and defer there, before anything is
powered up.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index f1fa6b2..0ab6b9d 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3041,6 +3041,22 @@ static int ufs_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	else
 		vops = &ufs_hba_qcom_vops;
 
+	/*
+	 * The PHY takes its reset from this controller, so fw_devlink sees a
+	 * cycle and does not hold this probe back until the PHY has bound.
+	 * Check for the PHY before ufshcd_pltfrm_init(): that powers up the
+	 * host's regulators and clocks, and a probe that then defers in
+	 * ufs_qcom_init() turns them back off, while blocks the bootloader
+	 * left running may share those clock sources.
+	 */
+	if (!has_acpi_companion(dev)) {
+		struct phy *phy = phy_get(dev, "ufsphy");
+
+		if (IS_ERR(phy))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(phy), "Failed to get PHY\n");
+		phy_put(dev, phy);
+	}
+
 	/* Perform generic probe */
 	err = ufshcd_pltfrm_init(pdev, vops);
 	if (err)
-- 
2.55.0

